+# Step 15-A frozen-engine checks
+
+These are opt-in synthetic technical-bundle checks, not live-provider tests.
+Run through the reviewed Step 13 Windows Python 3.14.7 browser/media Guard boundary.
+Do not invoke against an operating profile. STEP13_ROOT identifies a private test root;
+NEWSFLOW_VALIDATION_OUTPUT is a fresh evidence directory. NEWSFLOW_FFMPEG must be
+hash-pinned by that boundary. The frame test names the retained final probe `exe-probe6`.
+The GUI test requires the marked synthetic EXE server on 127.0.0.1:18765 with the probe's
+synthetic draft IDs; use a temporary Chrome profile and block non-local page requests.
+
+A Windows Job supervisor owns only the test tree. After checks, send CTRL_BREAK and
+require server_stop, exit 0, released port and zero active children before closing the Job.
+Forced failure cleanup is recorded separately and never counted as a normal-stop PASS.
+Keep the synthetic root to verify normal restart; do not re-execute paid or unknown jobs.
+The GUI check uses bounded Python polling for video playback to honor the existing CSP;
+no unsafe-eval exemption is needed. These files are outside ordinary tests/ collection.
+No profile, database, EXE, audio/video or private environment is stored in this repository.
